      en: "Siwa is a remarkable feature of the geography and culture of Egypt. An isolated oasis town near the Libyan border with a unique culture. Speak a Berber language. Site of the Oracle of Amun. This city is among the characteristic settlements of Egypt, often along the Nile or on the Red Sea coast. Like many notable places in Egypt, it links the pharaonic heritage with present-day life along the Nile. Thus, this place contributes to the diverse profile of Egypt between the Sahara, the Nile, the Suez Canal and the Red Sea.",
